  'angkor-wat-and-killing-fields-guided-halffull-day': {
    averageRating: 5.0,
    totalReviews: 9,
    guideRating: 5.0,
    valueRating: 5.0,
    reviews: [
      { author: "Andrew", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-23", text: "We have a fabulous tour of Angkor Wat and Killing Fields today. While the weather was not in our favour it did not stop the trip and the information Makara provided. The Killing Fields are a necessary visit to all so we learn this cannot happen again. Angkor Wat is overwhelming - the size, the construction and the design is immense. We had a fantastic afternoon and look forward to coming back for the next adventure." },
      { author: "Shelly", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-06", text: "I had the privilege of touring Angkor Wat and the Killing Fields with Mr. Pechey, and I can confidently say it was one of the most meaningful travel experiences I’ve ever had. As a former teacher, Mr. Pechey brings a rare depth of knowledge and clarity to his guiding. His approach felt less like a typical tour and more like a personal, professor-level journey through Cambodia’s history, culture, and soul. Every moment was thoughtful, intentional, and deeply educational. At Angkor Wat, he took the time to walk me through the intricate inscriptions and carvings, patiently explaining their meanin" },
      { author: "Alexander", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-02", text: "Great informative guide with a vast knowledge of Cambodian history. I enjoyed this tour, which was a private tour and started with a somber visit to the Killing Fields Siem Reap (Genocide Museum) and ended with enjoying the views at sunset from the Phnom Krom hill and First Angkor Temple." },
      { author: "Ellie", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-24", text: "This was such an incredible trip! My tour guide PJ answered any questions I had, and was very knowledgeable and informative the whole time. Very happy with this private tour!" },
      { author: "Freya", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-03", text: "Probably the best tour we’ve ever been on. Tom reached out the day before to send me the link to buy the tickets on, as there are lots of scam websites. Tom was friendly throughout, so informative and explained everything in such detail but still in a way we could understand. He’s clearly an enthusiast and it’s lovely to see he’s passionate about the history. His English was great and never an issue, we understood perfectly! We were given plenty of cold water bottles and cold wipes to refresh ourselves after each stop. I didn’t know at the time of booking, but this is a private tour just for y" },
      { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-07", text: "Angkor Wat was amazing, an incredible experience. The Killing Field was profoundly moving, it serves as a reminder of the history of Cambodia and the hardship that was once endured" },
    ],
  },
