  'battambang-day-trip-return-to-siem-reap-or-continu': {
    averageRating: 4.88,
    totalReviews: 89,
    guideRating: 4.86,
    valueRating: 4.71,
    reviews: [
      { author: "Gail", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-17", text: "we enjoyed our tour with Lucky he was a wonderful guide with great knowledge and able to answer all our questions and attend to our needs." },
      { author: "Aparna", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-05", text: "very Lovejoy drive n places. our guide Lucky was very sweet as d helpful. very pleased with the tour." },
      { author: "Sandra", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-04", text: "Great guide, good knowledge, also he is a great driver and very comfortable car! :)" },
      { author: "Sebastian", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-31", text: "This trip was amazing the tour guide was lovely. He was very helpful and caring always making sure we have plenty of water. He was extremely friendly and tried to answer all of our questions to the best of his ability. Over all the trip was very enjoyable and interesting" },
      { author: "Suzanne", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-17", text: "Lucky was an excellent guide, the description of the vehicle being business class is absolutely correct. we were driven at a good pace, the bamboo train was great fun. The bats were amazing. We had a very enjoyable trip." },
      { author: "Alessandro", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-13", text: "We were very happy with Lucky as a driver and a guide. Definitely a good solution if you intend visiting battambang but don’t have enough days for staying over. Fresh and deep-fried rolls were the best tried in cambodia, with handmade rice papers. Loved also the bat cave and the killing fields visit. Lowlight of the day was the bamboo train, felt very touristic and i would have skipped if i had to go again. Again, bug bonus star for Lucky, he was amazing." },
      { author: "Jane", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-11", text: "A great, very full-on day. We were picked up at 8:30am from Siem Reap and returned around 9:30pm. The journey was about three hours each way, but Lucky’s vehicle was amazing – the seats were like armchairs with leg rests and even a massage function, which made the trip very comfortable. Although it wasn’t advertised as a private tour, it ended up being just the two of us, which was a lovely bonus. We saw everything on the itinerary and also visited a family making banana chips and rice paper. We were able to try both and there was no pressure to buy anything. The timing was perfect to watch th" },
      { author: "Christina", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-22", text: "Lucky was a fabulous guide and his luxury vehicle was like travelling business class! He will go at your pace and you can add or skip things along the way. We found the variety of activities a great mix - highlights were the bamboo train and the bats flying out of the cave. Good to get away from the more touristy areas too. Highly recommend." },
      { author: "Mya", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-19", text: "\"Highly recommend this private tour with Lucky! We had a spacious seven-seater van for just three people, making the 3-hour drive from Siem Reap very comfortable. Lucky was punctual, knowledgeable, and his English is great. He even made an impromptu stop at a local market for us. The highlight was definitely the Bat Cave. Despite a delay at the Bamboo Train, Lucky timed our arrival perfectly so we could see the spectacular sight of thousands of bats flying out at dusk. He got us back to Siem Reap safely and we couldn't be happier with his service!\"" },
      { author: "Agnieszka", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-15", text: "Exceptional Day Trip with Lucky! Battambang's Best Guide! Lucky made my day trip from Siem Reap to Battambang absolutely unforgettable. His knowledge of the region and genuine care made me feel safe while having an authentic adventure. He guided me through Battambang's highlights - stunning temples, the sobering killing caves, local villages, and the thrilling bamboo train. What really stood out was Lucky introducing me to incredible local fruits and traditional foods I'd never have discovered on my own. Transportation was super comfortable - air-conditioned vehicle for the full day. Lucky sho" },
      { author: "andrew", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-15", text: "it was an excellent trip. Great value for money. got to see many sights and activities. our driver Lucky was excellent. Great Englush, very knowledgeable and friendly. Vehicle was extremely comfortable. Cannot recommend this trip and guide highly enough." },
      { author: "Gemma", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-14", text: "Lucky was great from start to finish. It’s a long day but more than doable. Lucky’s van was so comfortable and spacious, he provided fresh water throughout the day and even added a few activities such as trying local fruit because the bats were to be coming out a little later than usual. Lucky was informative and provided us information about where we were going and what we were seeing. 10/10 recommend this trip to see Battambang in one day and especially with Lucky. Thank you!" },
    ],
  },
