  'siem-reap-road-transfer-plus-sightseeing': {
    averageRating: 4.91,
    totalReviews: 196,
    guideRating: 4.93,
    valueRating: 4.65,
    reviews: [
      { author: "Anton", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-03", text: "Great trip with guide Polen. The ride was comfortable, and the guide told interesting stories." },
      { author: "Julian", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-30", text: "Great - we saw a lot on the trip and it was good to see the countryside" },
      { author: "Paul", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-28", text: "Excellent - knowledgable and helpful guide, enjoyed our activities, very polite, respectful driver and very flexible too." },
      { author: "Nick", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-24", text: "Raman was amazing from start to finish - car was incredibly comfy for 4 adults with luggage, great explanations, well versed in local culture, destinations were well chosen. Temple at Prasat Sambour Prei Kuk a hidden gem, and fishing village was eye-opening. A wonderful way to get from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap." },
      { author: "Slavica", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-02", text: "We had an excellent driver named Thet, he was very considerate and modified our trip to suit our needs. He found great places to stop along the way and was very knowledgeable. The water village was unlike anything we’ve seen before and was very educational visiting such a place. We highly recommended him as a guide and driver." },
      { author: "Louisa", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-05", text: "An excellent day. Thearak drove carefully and spoke excellent English. He was very knowledgeable about Cambodian history and very willing to share his knowledge on the long drive to Siam Reap helping us understand the complex ancient and more recent history. The temple stop with a local guide was excellent and we stopped soon after for a delicious lunch by the lake with good recommendations from Thearak. We then stopped at the ancient bridge and were again given a full explanation from Thearak and finally stopped at Kampong Kleang fishing village . It was the end of the dry season so you could" },
      { author: "Roswitha", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-27", text: "The journey from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap was brilliant. Our driver (I think his name was Mr Zing) gave us lots of information during the rather long drive. Several stops were planned. All the stops were excellent. Mr Zing looked after us very well and showed us lots of beautiful spots (especially at the fishing village of Kompong Khleang on Tonle Sap Lake). At our request, he also stopped briefly at interesting spots so we could take photos. Thank you very much! It was a very successful day." },
      { author: "Rachel", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-09", text: "We had a great time with our guide sam and driver James! Wonderful scenery and the waterfall was incredible. Our guide was very knowledgable and we would definitely recommend this tour!" },
      { author: "Mark", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-02", text: "Absolutely fantastic tour. The stops were very interesting and my guide was spot on. Very good English and his information and insights were very good." },
      { author: "Zoe", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-28", text: "We had a wonderful day travelling from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap and seeing some really great parts of Cambodia along the way. Our guide Thearak was super friendly and spoke excellent English and was super easy to understand. He had an incredible knowledge of Cambodia and was able to tell us all about its history and day to day life here. All of the stops were fun and interesting, good value, and the car was very comfortable with good air conditioning even though it was quite a hot day." },
      { author: "Michael", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-27", text: "What a great way to transfer between Siem Reap and Phnon Penh! Our tourguide Thearak was amazing! He had so much knowledge about Cambodia and its history and spoke brilliant English. My wife who is not a native speaker really appreciated this as she normally struggles to understand local tour guides accents. Thank you so much Thearak for a great experience!" },
      { author: "Simon", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-24", text: "Brilliant day. Our guide Thearak spoke excellent English and was so knowledgable about the history of Cambodia. It is a long day but broken up nicely by some amazing visits. He also found an excellent spot for lunch with amazing food. It really was a great experience especially the floating village which gave you an insight into the rural community of the Country. Nice comfortable car with cold towels and plenty of water. Would recommend to all of you are visiting Siem Reap and Phnom Penh, so much better than flying and missing so much to see. Perfect!!!" },
    ],
  },
